### Page 3 of 5

```text
jurisdictional acceptance of any properly permitted improvements.
The boundary lines of said temporary construction easement shall be lengthened
or shortened to maintain a continuous 20 foot wide temporary construction
easement on each side of the access easement, extending from the North line of
Block 15 to the South line of East Murray Road right-of-way.
GRANTOR grants this access easement in anticipation of the replat of Lots 100 and 200,
Sweetgrass, 6 Filing, for which access is required across lands owned by GRANTOR.
GRANTOR further grants to the GRANTEE the right to enter upon said land and the
right to use and maintain any and all structures, appurtenances, and fixtures along said access.
GRANTOR further grants to the GRANTEE the right to ingress and egress from the
above-described land and covenant that it shall, in no way, hinder or prevent the proper and
reasonable use and enjoyment of said property for access.
GRANTOR shall be responsible for construction and maintenance of improvements
within the access easement and improvements shall be constructed to the specifications as
defined and adopted by the City.
In the event of an excavation in the above-described access easement by the GRANTOR,
the GRANTOR shall be responsible to backfill and grade such right-of-way to the specifications
as defined and adopted by the City, and any costs for said restoration of improvements shall be
borne by the GRANTEE, its successors and assigns.
However, the GRANTOR shall not be
required to restore any improvements, such as pavement or vegetation.
Any costs for
restoration beyond backfill and grading shall be borne by the GRANTEE, its successors and
assigns.
The rights granted herein shall forever be subject to the rights of GRANTOR, its assigns
or lessees to explore for, develop, and extract any and all minerals or other subsurface resources
beneath this access easement.
If required for mineral exploration, development, or extraction,
the GRANTEE shall, upon written notice from the GRANTOR, remove or relocate the
above-described assets at its own expense.
Upon abandonment or discontinuance of use of the access easement for the purposes
specified above, all of GRANTEE’S rights under this grant of access easement shall revert to
GRANTOR or its successors or assigns, the same as if this grant had never been made.
Should
this access easement be abandoned by the GRANTEE, or GRANTEE’S successors or assigns,
the above-described tract of land shall be returned to a condition satisfactory to the landowner.
The access easement may be transferred; however, no transfer may increase the burden
on the servient estate in any manner.
Any transfer of ownership of this access easement, or any
change of name or mailing address of the owner of this access easement, shall be reported to the
GRANTOR within thirty (30) days of the transfer or change.
2
